# Task: Design the MCP Server Specification for the Enterprise Knowledge Platform

## Context

We have already completed and approved the following architecture:

- Knowledge Model
- PostgreSQL + pgvector schema
- Repository Analyzer
- Ingestion Pipeline
- Retrieval & Context Engine
- Knowledge Engine

Please use these documents as the source of truth.

Do NOT redesign any existing architecture.

---

## Objective

Design the MCP Server specification.

The MCP Server is an integration layer over the Knowledge Engine.

Its responsibility is ONLY to expose the Knowledge Engine capabilities as MCP Tools.

It must never contain:

- SQL
- Vector Search
- Business Logic
- Ranking
- Context Building
- Relationship Traversal
- LLM calls

All of these responsibilities belong to the Knowledge Engine.

---

## Important

Do NOT design MCP tools from database tables.

Do NOT expose CRUD APIs.

Do NOT expose internal database IDs as the primary interface.

The MCP interface must be designed around BUSINESS USE CASES.

---

## AI Workers

The following AI Workers will consume the MCP Server.

1. Impact Analysis Worker
2. Requirement Analysis Worker
3. OAS Generator
4. Repository Explorer
5. Architecture Assistant
6. Knowledge Explorer

---

## Your task

For each AI Worker,

identify

- what information it needs
- what operations it performs
- what context it requires

Then design the MINIMUM set of MCP tools required to support all workers.

Avoid duplicate tools.

Avoid CRUD tools unless absolutely necessary.

Prefer task-oriented tools.

---

